// A sibling of members/finalClassAddsOverride with the caller in the file of the base class.
// B is final and has no own override of foo, so b.foo() in a.kt is devirtualized into a direct
// call of A.foo, which is declared in a.kt itself. The per-file cache of a.kt therefore records
// no dependency at all on sub.kt, the file declaring B, whose member set decided the
// devirtualization target. When the final class B gets its own override of foo(), the IR of a.kt
// stays the same, but its cache must be rebuilt to call B.foo() instead of A.foo().

MODULES: lib, main

STEP 0:
    libs: lib, main

STEP 1:
    libs: lib, main
